concepts.body:
When a value can be computed from other state, declare it with **`$derived`**:

```js
let count = $state(0);
let doubled = $derived(count * 2);
```

Svelte tracks which state the expression reads and recalculates it when one of those changes. Derived values are **lazy and cached**: recomputed only when read after a dependency changed.

For logic that needs statements, use **`$derived.by`** with a function:

```js
let stats = $derived.by(() => {
  let done = 0;
  for (const t of todos) if (t.done) done++;
  return { done, open: todos.length - done };
});
```

Rules and tips:

- The expression must be free of side effects; Svelte disallows state changes inside a derived.
- Dependencies are whatever is read **synchronously** inside it.
- If the new value is identical (`===`) to the old one, dependents don't update.
- Since Svelte 5.25 you can temporarily **assign** to a derived (for optimistic UI); it recalculates again when its dependencies change.

The common mistake from other frameworks is to use an effect that writes to another `$state` whenever something changes. If you can express a value as a function of other state, `$derived` is simpler, faster and never out of sync.

Runes work in **`.svelte.js` / `.svelte.ts` modules**, so shared state can live outside components:

```js
// cart.svelte.js
export const cart = $state({ items: [] });
export function add(item) { cart.items.push(item); }
```

Any component importing `cart` sees the same reactive object. One rule: you **can't export a `$state` variable that you reassign** (`export let count = $state(0)` then `count++` elsewhere won't propagate), because importers receive the value, not the binding. Export an object and mutate its properties, or export getter functions.

**Classes** are a clean way to bundle state with behaviour: fields declared with `$state`/`$derived` become reactive accessors.

Module-level state is a **singleton per process**. In a server-rendered app that means it is shared between all users' requests, so never keep per-user data there. Use **context** instead: `setContext(key, value)` in a parent during initialisation and `getContext(key)` in any descendant. Context is scoped to the component tree, so on the server each request gets its own. Svelte 5.40+ adds **`createContext()`**, which returns typed get and set functions (plus a has check) and avoids string keys.

Put a `$state` object (or class instance) in context so descendants see updates. Svelte stores (`writable`, `$store` syntax) still work and remain useful for streams of values, but runes cover most shared-state needs.

concepts.code:
// counter.svelte.js
export class Counter {
  count = $state(0);
  double = $derived(this.count * 2);
  increment = () => { this.count++; };   // arrow keeps `this` when passed around
}
export const globalCounter = new Counter();   // singleton (careful with SSR)

// session.js - per-tree state via context (Svelte 5.40+)
import { createContext } from 'svelte';
export const [getSession, setSession] = createContext();

// Layout.svelte <script>
//   import { setSession } from './session.js';
//   let { user, children } = $props();
//   setSession({ get user() { return user; } });   // stays reactive

// Avatar.svelte <script> (any depth below)
//   import { getSession } from './session.js';
//   import { globalCounter } from './counter.svelte.js';
//   const session = getSession();
//   <button onclick={globalCounter.increment}>{session.user.name} {globalCounter.double}</button>

// src/routes/todos/+page.server.js
import { fail } from '@sveltejs/kit';
import { db } from '$lib/server/db';         // server-only module

export async function load() {
  return { todos: await db.todos.all() };     // becomes `data` in the page
}

export const actions = {
  default: async ({ request }) => {
    const text = (await request.formData()).get('text');
    if (!text) return fail(400, { missing: true });
    await db.todos.add(String(text));
  },
};

// src/routes/todos/+page.svelte
// <script>
//   import { enhance } from '$app/forms';
//   let { data, form } = $props();
// </script>
// <form method="POST" use:enhance>
//   <input name="text" />{#if form?.missing}<p>Required</p>{/if}
// </form>
// {#each data.todos as t (t.id)}<p>{t.text}</p>{/each}

// What the compiler roughly produces for:
//   <script> let count = $state(0); let double = $derived(count * 2); </script>
//   <button onclick={() => count++}>{count} x2 = {double}</button>
// (Svelte 5.57 output, lightly trimmed; internals change between versions)

import * as $ from 'svelte/internal/client';
var root = $.from_html(`<button> </button>`);     // parsed once, cloned per instance

export default function App($$anchor) {
  let count = $.state(0);                           // source signal
  let double = $.derived(() => $.get(count) * 2);   // lazy computed signal
  var button = root();
  var text = $.only_child(button);
  $.template_effect(() =>                           // fine-grained effect for one text node
    $.set_text(text, `${$.get(count) ?? ''} x2 = ${$.get(double) ?? ''}`));
  $.delegated('click', button, () => $.update(count));   // delegated click handler
  $.append($$anchor, button);
}
$.delegate(['click']);

// Runtime model: $.set marks dependents dirty (push), deriveds recompute when read (pull),
// and effects are flushed together in a microtask (flushSync() forces it).

// embed.svelte.js - mounting Svelte inside a non-Svelte page or a test
import { mount, unmount, flushSync } from 'svelte';
import Counter from './Counter.svelte';

const props = $state({ start: 5 });              // reactive props object
const counter = mount(Counter, { target: document.querySelector('#widget'), props });
flushSync();                                     // DOM is now rendered
console.log(document.querySelector('#widget').textContent);   // e.g. "count: 5"

props.start = 10;                                // component reacts to prop change
counter.reset?.();                               // call a function the component exported
await unmount(counter, { outro: true });         // play outros, then remove

